# Card-driven delivery audit: triggers on each card in `Ready` that has NOT
# been audited yet. The auditor is VERDICT-ONLY: it posts a control-verdict
# comment + adds the control:audited label — it never moves cards or touches
# issue state. The card stays in `Ready`; the HUMAN routes it (Done = accept,
# Approved = rework; tal strips the label at rework start, so re-deliveries
# re-enter this queue automatically).
# Closed issues are NOT audited: a human closing directly has already routed —
# same philosophy as the label-by-hand waiver.
AGENT="test-automation-lead"
STATUS_ACTIVE=""        # verdict-only: no In Progress retry query
SID_SCOPE="control"      # own conversation namespace not to collide with another test automation lead, not needed for cardless, needed for card-driven
STATUS_READY="Ready"                # trigger column: agent-terminal deliveries
QUERY="-label:control:audited"      # only unaudited cards; the label — not a
                                    # card move — is what takes a case out of
                                    # this queue (negation verified)
POLL="10h"                          # empty-queue recheck cadence only
MAX_TURNS=""                        # optional cap, as everywhere
# EXCLUSIVE not needed: read-only on git, writes only comments + one label
# WORKDIR not needed: never touches a working tree
